<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>rs-rich-doom: third-party notices</title>
<style>
body { font-family: sans-serif; max-width: 60em; margin: 2em auto; padding: 0 1em; }
pre { white-space: pre-wrap; background: #f4f4f4; padding: 1em; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Third-party notices</h1>
<p>rs-rich-doom's binaries include the Rust crates below, under these
licences. The C code built into them is in the source: the Doom engine
(<code>doomgeneric/</code>, GPL-2.0-or-later), Chocolate Doom's OPL code
(<code>opl/</code>, GPL-2.0-or-later) and Nuked OPL3 (<code>opl/opl3.*</code>,
LGPL-2.1-or-later). The binaries are distributed under GPL-3.0-or-later
(LICENSE-GPL-3.0); see docs/licensing.md.</p>
<h2>Licences used</h2>
<ul>
{{#each overview}}
<li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> ({{count}})</li>
{{/each}}
</ul>
<h2>Licence texts</h2>
{{#each licenses}}
<h3 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h3>
<p>Used by:</p>
<ul>
{{#each used_by}}
<li><a href="{{#if crate.repository}}{{crate.repository}}{{else}}https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}}{{/if}}">{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</a></li>
{{/each}}
</ul>
<pre>{{text}}</pre>
{{/each}}
</body>
</html>
